 "text": "..title\nA resolution authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, acting by and through Metro Water Services, to enter into a Facility Encroachment Agreement with CSX TRANSPORTATION, INC. to construct, use and maintain culverts in the railroad right-of-way at Reeves Road and Goodwin Road, in Davidson County, (Project No. 27-SWD-050 and Proposal No. 2026M057AG-001).  \n..body\nWHEREAS, The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, through Metro Water Services (“Licensee”) desires to construct, or cause to be constructed, use and maintain, one 14 inch by 23 inch by 40 inch elliptical RCP culvert and culvert headwall solely for the conveyance of stormwater over, under, or across property owned or controlled by CSX TRANSPORTATION, INC. (“Licensor”), pursuant to the terms of the Facility Encroachment Agreement (TN085 CSX1043077), attached hereto in substantial form as Exhibit 1, and,\nWHEREAS, Licensee shall pay Licensor a one-time nonrefundable Encroachment Fee of One and 00/100 Dollars ($1.00) upon execution of this contract; and,\nWHEREAS, Resolution No. RS2022-1465 authorized The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to enter agreements with CSX Transportation, Inc. by resolution; and,\nWHEREAS, approval of this agreement will benefit the citizens of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County. \nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Facility Encroachment Agreement, attached hereto in substantial form as Exhibit 1 and incorporated herein by reference, is hereby approved, and that the Metropolitan Mayor is authorized to execute the same.\nSection 2.\tThat this resolution shall take effect from and after its adoption, the welfare of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis resolution authorizes the Metropolitan Department of Water and Sewerage Services (“MWS”) to enter into a facility encroachment agreement with CSX Transportation, Inc. (“CSX”).\n\nThe agreement allows NDOT to install a 14 inch by 23 inch by 40 inch elliptical RCP culvert and culvert headwall solely to convey stormwater over, under, or across property owned or controlled by CSX in the railroad right-of-way at Reeves Road and Goodwin Road. MWS would pay a one-time nonrefundable encroachment fee of $1.\n\nFiscal Note: The Department of Water and Sewerage Services (“MWS”) will pay a one-time nonrefundable encroachment fee in the amount of $1.00 to CSX Transportation, Inc. to construct one 14 inches by 23 inches by 40 inches elliptical RCP culvert and culvert headwall.\n\n"
}
